## Final edit prompt

Refine this existing polar UV cloud painting. Keep exactly its cloud distribution, clear center and orientation. Improve painted shading quality significantly. INWARD FACING CROWNS: highest richness of fine hand-painted shading and delicate irregular brushwork, several scales of soft volumes and light transitions, clean detailed silhouette, bright connected white planes. No outlined rims, no repeated popcorn/scallops, no sawtooth spikes. INTERIOR: medium detail, visibly worked painterly density with subtle overlapping brush touches and soft low-contrast shadow pockets, retain large coherent masses but NOT empty flat blobs, NOT Gaussian smearing, NOT a smooth gradient. The crown is most detailed, interior gently less detailed, outward base softest. Elegant anime matte-painting gouache craftsmanship. Respect radial orientation everywhere especially small northwest banks: bright crown southeast toward center, shadowed base northwest outward; northeast crown southwest; north crown down. Cloud flow is tangent to concentric circles, never a spiral. Keep genuine transparent sky and softly fading outward base alpha. Opaque shadowed interiors, transparency only where cloud density dissipates at edges. No black or white background, no colored fringe, no speckle halo, no checkerboard painted into image, no text. Keep original square framing and all black-empty-source-sky areas transparent. Refine BOTH small distant banks and large banks; distant shadows subtle but readable.
